{"id":"hv_kvp_daemon.8","n":"hv_kvp_daemon","s":"8","src":{"u":{"pkg":"linux-cloud-tools-common","ver":"5.15.0-204.214","repo":"jammy-updates/main","url":"http://archive.ubuntu.com/ubuntu/pool/main/l/linux/linux-cloud-tools-common_5.15.0-204.214_all.deb","path":"/usr/share/man/man8/hv_kvp_daemon.8.gz","sha256":"71e7a51465959cce295955acfca10ccea3adf9a1f1199def83bf7a6e3092c526","date":"","origin":"","also":["linux-intel-iotg-cloud-tools-common"]}},"nopt":{"u":0},"desc":"Hyper-V Key Value Pair daemon","u":[["NAME","<p>hv_kvp_daemon - Hyper-V Key Value Pair daemon</p>"],["SYNOPSIS","<p><b>hv_kvp_daemon</b></p>"],["DESCRIPTION","<p><b>hv_kvp_daemon</b> is the userspace component of the Hyper-V key value pair functionality, communicating via a netlink socket with the kernel HV-KVP driver. This pairing allows the Hyper-V host to pass configuration information (such as IP addresses) to the guest and allows the host to obtain guest version information.</p>"],["FILES","<pre>/var/opt/hyperv/.kvp_pool_*</pre>"],["AUTHORS","<pre>Written by K. Y. Srinivasan &lt;ksrinivasan@novell.com&gt;</pre>"]]}